Message:
refactor(Wind): Prune orphaned Effect-TS imports from de-Effectified service domains

Remove the final dangling Effect-TS import statements (Effect, Layer, Stream, Either, Context) from stub, mock, live, and layer files across seven service domains — Commands, Editor, Extensions, Output, Sandbox, Sidebar, and TextModelResolver — whose interfaces and implementations were already converted to native async/sync signatures in prior commits (f97e5dd, ae82728, ff60a11, 1621bf7).

Each affected file carried an import for a type or function that no longer appeared in its active code paths:
- Stub files (CommandsStub, OutputStub, TextModelResolverStub): strip the orphaned { Effect } import
- Mock files (CommandsMock, ExtensionsMock, OutputMock, TextModelResolverMock): strip { Layer } import
- Live implementations (OutputLive, TextModelResolverLive): strip { Effect, Layer } / { Effect } import
- Layer composition files (Electron, Tauri, Test): strip { Layer } import from the top-level layer barrel
- Interface files (OutputService, SandboxService, SidebarService): strip import type { Effect } / { Effect, Stream }
- Problem type files (CommandsProblem, EditorProblem, ExtensionsProblem): strip import type { Effect }
- Sandbox layer files (SandboxLive, SandboxMock): strip { Context, Effect, Layer } / { Effect, Layer }
- Sidebar layer files (SidebarLive, SidebarMock): strip { Effect, Either, Layer, Stream } / { Effect, Layer, Stream }
- Clipboard barrel: prune the now-unused Effect-related re-exports

Impact: Zero dead Effect-TS import traces remain across all Wind service domains that have been fully migrated to native async/sync. This completes the import-level cleanup phase of the de-Effectification sweep.
